# The README logo is a repo-only asset: it makes the GitHub page look right and
# is of no use to anyone installing the module. `git archive` honours
# export-ignore, and that is what the module zip is built from, so this keeps
# the image out of `go install` without touching the repo layout.
#
# scripts/check-module-zip.sh asserts the image is absent from the tag export,
# so deleting this line fails CI instead of quietly shipping the file.
images/ export-ignore
